.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt MICROINIT 8
.Os "BigFred OS"
.Sh NAME
.Nm microinit
.Nd system init and service supervisor for BigFred OS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm init
.Op Fl -logs-tty Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -init-logs-tty Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -console Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -config Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -no-early-boot
.Op Fl -allow-no-early-boot
.Op Fl -log-to-files
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm supervise
.Op Fl -console Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -config Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -log-to-files
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm start
.Op Fl -force
.Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm stop|restart|enable|disable
.Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm list
.Op Fl -show-labels
.Op Fl -selector Ns = Ns Ar key=value
.Op Fl l Ar key=value
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm describe
.Op Fl o Ar human|json
.Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar path
.Cm logs
.Op Ar name
.Op Fl -follow
.Op Fl -lines Ns = Ns Ar N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a PID 1 init system that loads a declarative JSON service list, starts
services (foreground sequentially, background in parallel), supervises
daemons with optional restart/backoff, and exposes a Unix-socket control
API used by the same binary's management subcommands.
.Pp
.Cm supervise
uses the same runtime as
.Cm init
but skips early-boot, getty, TTY attach, late unmount, and machine reboot
.Pq suitable for containers / distroless images ;
on shutdown it only stops services, syncs, and exits.
.Pp
When invoked as
.Pa /sbin/init
or as PID 1 without a subcommand,
.Nm
automatically enters
.Cm init
mode.
.Ss Boot sequence
.Bl -enum
.It
Run early-boot script
.Xr early-boot.sh 8
.Pq on-disk override/base, else embedded portable script; skipped by supervise
.It
Create or load
.Xr microinit.json 5 ,
merge drop-ins under
.Pa $DATA_DIR/etc/microinit.d/services/ ,
and apply
.Xr microinit.services.enabled-override.json 5
.It
Topologically sort services by
.Cm dependsOn
.It
Start enabled services; print
.Bq OK
/
.Bq FAIL
on the console
.It
Write microinit operational logs to the init-logs TTY
.Pq default Pa /dev/tty3 ; skipped when TTY attach is disabled
.It
Respawn getty on the console TTY
.Pq init only, when PID 1
.It
Watch config JSON via inotify and reload services
.It
Supervise processes, reap zombies, serve IPC
.El
.Pp
TTY roles:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Pa /dev/tty1
.Pq Fl -console
— boot status
.Bq OK
/
.Bq FAIL
and login getty
.It
.Pa /dev/tty2
.Pq Fl -logs-tty
— mixed service stdout/stderr
.It
.Pa /dev/tty3
.Pq Fl -init-logs-tty
— microinit's own runtime log
.Pq start/stop/restart/enable, crashes, IPC actions
; survives login on the console
.El
.Pp
All lines are kept in fixed-capacity in-memory ring buffers
.Pq Cm logs.lines
and are available via
.Cm microinit logs .
File append under
.Cm logs.dir
is off by default
.Pq Cm logs.logToFiles false
; enable with
.Fl -log-to-files
or
.Cm logs.logToFiles true .
.Pp
During boot, operational messages are written both to the console/stderr and to
.Fl -init-logs-tty .
After
.Dq boot complete ,
lifecycle events
.Pq Cm start , Cm stop , Cm restart , enable/disable, crash restarts
appear only on
.Fl -init-logs-tty
so the login console stays clean.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGTERM , SIGINT
Ordered shutdown then reboot
.It Dv SIGUSR1
Halt
.It Dv SIGUSR2
Power off
.It Dv SIGCHLD
Reap exited children
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /data/etc/microinit.services.enabled-override.json
.It Pa /data/etc/microinit.json
Main configuration
.It Pa /data/etc/microinit.json.example
Example configuration written on first boot
.It Pa /data/etc/microinit.services.enabled-override.json
Per-service
.Cm enabled
overrides
.It Pa /etc/microinit/early-boot.sh
Early-boot script
.It Pa /data/etc/microinit/early-boot.sh
Optional early-boot override
.It Pa /etc/microinit/unmount.sh
Late-shutdown unmount script
.It Pa /data/etc/microinit/unmount.sh
Optional unmount override
.It Pa /data/run/microinit.sock
Control socket
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
microinit init --logs-tty=/dev/tty2 --init-logs-tty=/dev/tty3
microinit list
microinit list --show-labels
microinit list -l created-by=bigfred
microinit describe redis
microinit describe -o json redis
microinit start redis
microinit start --force alloy
microinit restart redis
microinit logs alloy --follow
microinit disable dropbear
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm list
supports
.Fl -show-labels
to print a
.Cm LABELS
column, and repeatable
.Fl l / Fl -selector
.Pq form Cm key=value
to keep only services matching all selectors
.Pq AND .
.Cm describe
always prints labels, the live process identity
.Pq Cm Running as
from
.Pa /proc
,
and the configured
.Cm securityContext
.Pq Cm Security
on Linux .
.Fl o Ar json
prints the raw service object from its source drop-in or main config file
.Pq stdout is pure JSON; the source path goes to stderr .
.Pp
.Cm start
prints a status line on stdout: either that the service is starting, that it is
.Cm waiting_for_dependency ,
or
.Pq with Fl -force
that it is starting despite unmet dependencies.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr microinit.json 5 ,
.Xr microinit.services.enabled-override.json 5 ,
.Xr early-boot.sh 8 ,
.Xr unmount.sh 8 ,
.Xr shutdown 8
